# Pinned toolchain and dependency versions.
#
# Sourced by every build script and by the GitHub workflows. Editing this file
# changes the "build key", which makes the upstream poller publish a new release
# even when the OpenVPN version itself has not moved.
#
# Every value uses ${VAR:-default} so it can be overridden from the environment
# (the workflows do this for their manual-dispatch inputs).

# --- Android toolchain -------------------------------------------------------

# NDK revision, as it appears in the Google download URL:
#   https://dl.google.com/android/repository/android-ndk-<NDK_VERSION>-linux.zip
# r28c is stable, enables 16 KB page alignment by default, and still supports
# minSdkVersion 21. NDK r26..r30 all support API 21; the raise to API 23 cannot
# land before r31 (android/ndk#2188).
NDK_VERSION="${NDK_VERSION:-r28c}"

# Minimum supported Android API level. 21 = Android 5.0 Lollipop.
API_LEVEL="${API_LEVEL:-21}"

# ABIs to build. arm64-v8a and x86_64 are 64-bit only, which requires API 21
# upwards anyway.
ABIS="${ABIS:-armeabi-v7a arm64-v8a x86 x86_64}"

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------

# OpenSSL LTS line. The exact patch release is resolved at build time to the
# newest tag on this line (see resolve-versions.sh). Set a full version here
# instead (e.g. 3.5.7) to freeze it completely.
OPENSSL_LINE="${OPENSSL_LINE:-3.5}"

# https://www.oberhumer.com/opensource/lzo/
LZO_VERSION="${LZO_VERSION:-2.10}"

# https://github.com/lz4/lz4/releases
LZ4_VERSION="${LZ4_VERSION:-1.10.0}"

# --- OpenVPN -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Fallback upstream tag. Normally resolve-versions.sh replaces this with the
# newest stable release on the highest X.Y line.
OPENVPN_TAG="${OPENVPN_TAG:-v2.7.5}"
